WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.135
NARRATOR: A suspicious message tries to
collapse the time between reading and acting.

2
00:00:05.135 --> 00:00:06.209
NARRATOR: Pause.

3
00:00:06.209 --> 00:00:11.515
NARRATOR: Look for urgency, emotional
pressure, an unexpected attachment, a request

4
00:00:11.515 --> 00:00:17.785
for private information, or a sender address
that only resembles the real organization.

5
00:00:17.785 --> 00:00:21.861
NARRATOR: One red flag is not proof, but it is
a reason to stop.

6
00:00:21.962 --> 00:00:25.879
NARRATOR: Do not use the message itself to
prove the message is legitimate.

7
00:00:25.879 --> 00:00:31.397
NARRATOR: Instead, open the organization's
known website, use a saved phone number, or

8
00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:34.792
start a fresh message to a trusted contact.

9
00:00:34.792 --> 00:00:38.447
NARRATOR: Check the full destination and
sender carefully.

10
00:00:38.447 --> 00:00:43.066
NARRATOR: Independent verification breaks the
attacker's control of the path.

11
00:00:43.178 --> 00:00:48.174
NARRATOR: If the message remains suspicious,
report it using your organization's approved

12
00:00:48.174 --> 00:00:51.089
process or your email provider's phishing
control.

13
00:00:51.089 --> 00:00:54.622
NARRATOR: Then delete it without opening links
or attachments.

14
00:00:54.622 --> 00:00:58.100
NARRATOR: Reporting helps defenders protect
other recipients.

15
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:04.160
NARRATOR: The safe sequence is pause, verify
independently, report, and remove.
